{
  "$comment": [
    "Human-maintained build inputs for scripts/build-resources.mjs.",
    "Maps catalog id (data/models.json models[].id) -> Hugging Face repo, plus overrides.",
    "Generated output lives in data/model-resources.json and is owned entirely by the CLI.",
    "See docs/plans/resource-constraints-pipeline.md (Phase 1) and docs/specs/resource-constraints.md.",
    "",
    "Every `hf` and `quantRepos` value below was probed against the Hub on 2026-08-28;",
    "quantRepos were confirmed against the full ibm-granite repo listing rather than",
    "assumed from a <repo>-GGUF naming rule, so an absent entry means no quant repo ships.",
    "",
    "The 4.2 series ships three non-GGUF first-party quantizations (-fp8, -mxfp4, -nvfp4)",
    "in addition to -GGUF. Each holds a single model.safetensors, so the CLI must derive",
    "the variant label from the repo suffix rather than the filename, and the GGUF-shaped",
    "`recommended`/`aggressive` label rules do not apply to them.",
    "The three 4.2 models have no editorial entry in models.json yet — the CLI's",
    "discrepancy report will flag them until one is added by hand.",
    "",
    "`companionRepos` lists checkpoints a composite model loads alongside its own",
    "weights at runtime, which are therefore resident for every variant. The Granite",
    "Switch models embed their adapters in the checkpoint (already measured), but pull",
    "the speech encoder from its own repo when `asr_enabled` is set. Companion bytes",
    "are added to every variant, full precision and quantized alike.",
    "See docs/plans/switch-addition-plan.md (section 2.3).",
    "The Switch `-preview` repos are deliberately not listed yet (plan section 7)."
  ],
